<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TOYOTA SOUTH AFRICA PLANT CLOSED BY STRIKE.</title>
<headline>TOYOTA SOUTH AFRICA PLANT CLOSED BY STRIKE.</headline>
<dateline>DURBAN 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota South Africa Ltd said its Prospecton plant was shut down on Monday and stood to lose 15 million rand in turnover because of a one-day strike called to protest against new labour legislation.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no production here at all. We have closed the plant...it means we will not put out 450 vehicles today which will in turn mean a loss of 15 million rand in cumulative turnover,&quot; Toyota spokesman Richard Wingfield told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Prospecton plant outside Durban employs a workforce of 5,500 people.</p>
<p>Normal production was expected to resume on Tuesday, he said.</p>
<p>--Durban Newsroom +27 31 306 8646</p>
</text>
